# Page Header Standard

Use one header format on every non-fullBleed screen (`layouts/main.php`):

1. **Left top:** breadcrumb `Home / {Page}`
2. **Left:** page title + provider chip (Cheerio/Meta)
3. **Right:** primary page actions (`header_actions` section)

## Body sections (below the header)

Wrap page content in `.page-list` (or `.page-stack`). Stack blocks with consistent gap (`--section-gap`):

1. **Filters** — one `.card` with `.filter-bar` (placeholders/`title`, not field labels)
2. **Hints** — slim `.page-hint` when needed (never a second toolbar)
3. **Main content** — `.card` with optional `.card-header` title, or `.dash-panel` for charts
4. **Named groups** — `.page-section` + `.page-section-title` for KPI/chart groups

## Do

- Put Create / Sync / Export / Refresh / New buttons in `<?= $this->section('header_actions') ?>`
- Keep filters, search, and secondary controls in the page body (card/filter bar)
- Keep one title only — never duplicate the page `h1` inside content
- Prefer `.page-list` gap over ad-hoc `mb-2` / `mb-3` between sections

## Don't

- Do not put primary actions in a separate `page-toolbar` under the title
- Do not right-align the breadcrumb
- Do not invent a second page title row
- Do not mix Bootstrap filter rows with `.filter-bar` on the same screen type

## Example

```php
<?= $this->extend('layouts/main') ?>

<?= $this->section('header_actions') ?>
<a href="<?= site_url('contacts/create') ?>" class="btn btn-wa btn-sm">Add contact</a>
<?= $this->endSection() ?>

<?= $this->section('content') ?>
<div class="page-list">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header"><h2 class="card-title mb-0">All contacts</h2></div>
    <div class="card-body py-3">
      <div class="filter-bar">...</div>
      <table>...</table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<?= $this->endSection() ?>
```
